/OidcPolicy":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is which is the whole of what [","type":"text"},{"code":"validate_tenant_override","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"clamp_overrides_to_org","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"], validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — the mirror image of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"mfa_enforced","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because releasing personal data is the less-restrictive direction, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant can turn its organization’s decision off but never on. *","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dynamic_registration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], on the ladder ","type":"text"},{"code":"disabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"initial_access_token","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" →","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymous","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": a tenant may move down it and never up. * [","type":"text"},